        "original_id": "2f15f45b-c3ee-5ba4-9ca1-1a0825f418f3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Songs: \"Walking in the Air\"\n- People: Howard Blake, Raymond Briggs, Peter Auty\n- Works: The Snowman\n- Organizations: St Paul's Cathedral, Stiff Records\n\nFacts:\n- Raymond Briggs wrote the children's book The Snowman in 1978.\n- Howard Blake wrote the song \"Walking in the Air\" for the 1982 animated film adaptation of Raymond Briggs' 1978 book The Snowman.\n- Peter Robert Auty was born on 4 November 1969.\n- In the 1982 film The Snowman, St Paul's Cathedral choirboy Peter Auty performed \"Walking in the Air\".\n- \"Walking in the Air\" was reissued in 1985 on Stiff Records and again in 1987.\n- Peter Auty is an English operatic tenor who has worked with most major opera companies in Britain and with a number of companies in continental Europe.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "97ed4c08-23cd-56ce-b46b-ba8b5a26d44a",
        "text": "Page: Walking in the Air. Sentence: \"Walking in the Air\" is a song written by Howard Blake for the 1982 animated film of Raymond Briggs' 1978 children's book \"The Snowman\".\nPage: Walking in the Air. Sentence: In the film, the song was performed by St Paul's Cathedral choirboy Peter Auty, and reissued in 1985 (on Stiff Records) and 1987.\nPage: Peter Auty. Sentence: Peter Robert Auty (born 4 November 1969) is an English operatic tenor who has worked with most of the major opera companies in Britain and a number of companies in continental Europe.",
